Well, the third Chris ascends, and another Valkerie joins the crowd in
DemiBar.

Like all games played on the Ipaq this one was random after the entry of
Chris as a name. I resolved to keep my usual conducts, geno and
polyless.  I also was a bit of a gem collector, not being able to resist
an ID'ed valuable gem type throughout the game.  This game was one where
I didn't make as many ?oEA as I might as my ending armor would show.  I
got mojo on an altar on level 5 then headed to the mines.  I lost
Polyself to a trap in the mines, another trap made Killer and PussPuss
(my dog and cat) into a Panther (not changing Puss's letter or needing a
name change) and a Master Mind Flayer who was quickly re-named Cthulu.
The elder god layed waste to many of the dungeon's inhabitants, although
he did not manage to open the locked door to the minetown lighting shop
or the small (3X3) temple on level 15 where I made my base for much of
the game.  I had speed boots and a robe (thanks to a purple h) but no MR
or reflection until after I beat medusa over the head with Thor's
sledgehammer. I substituted Perseus' sheild for my own and stashed the
Sokoban BoH in his sack.  (named curse cover at this point)  I got my
second sad feeling at this point as Cthulu it turned out was not a god
and was drowned by an eel.  Ghennom was needlessly strange and diffucult
thanks to a tap error in Orcustown that allowed an unfriendly purple h
to suck some of my brains.  I managed to get to the VS I dropped the
bell and candelabrum and then headed back to the Fakewiz and the portal.
The zoo contained another purple h who got shown Orcus' wand.

Once I woke Rodney the fun really started.  He double troubled right
away (first of four double troubles) and I had to beat them both to
death after discharging orcus' wand without hitting either one. (three
charges)  I did manage to get out with the book  The invocation went
fine even with a horse coming up as I was reading the book and
interrupting me once. (first time that's happened)  Downstairs in the
Sanctum, two Master Liches geeted me, one summoning nasties on turn two.
The purple & scared the hell out of me but when it turned out to be
Yeenoghu I breathed a sigh of relief I beat them all with Mojo and
headed in to get Rodney's bauble.  In the graveyard a chest yeilded a
much needed /oDeath that I put to use after using one charge of my /oSDD
to find the door to the temple of Moloch.  Rodney re-appeared at this
point and went after the priest.  I waited to line them both up from
outside the door and hit the preistess but not Rodney who promptly
grabbed the amulet and teleported back to the upstairs.  I killed him
along the way to the stairs thanks to being un-burdened and sipped the
first of three c!oGL to exit the sanctum.

The RNG laughed at my careful preperations by making the mysterious
force hit me at least 20 times... many times on levels not completly
re-mapped after the MF incident.  A demon summoned Geryon at some point,
I wasted him with no trouble.  I made sure to stop at the temple on
level 15 to make sure it was safe to pray.  I had made a cannibal
mistake along the way in ghennom, weak I killed a captain and ate him
instead of his ration.  Tyr had forgiven me.

The planes were un-remarkable, the portal on air taking the longest to
get to (opposite corner of the level from arrival point) and going
center on astral (my last /oDeath charge got Famine with one try)  I had
once again guessed right.  I whistled in my Guardian Angel, chatted with
the high priest and gave Tyr what he really wanted.

